    "id": "TRF-114",
    "normalizedRequirement": "The thruster must withstand the loads occurring when the design ice block defined in Table 6-3 impacts on the thruster body when the ship is sailing at a typical ice operating speed. Load cases for impact loads are given in Table 6-16. The contact geometry is estimated to be hemispherical in shape. If the actual contact geometry differs from the shape of the hemisphere, a sphere radius must be estimated so that the growth of the contact area as a function of penetration of ice corresponds as closely as possible to the actual geometrical shape penetration.",
    "page": 53,
    "requiredInputs": "No explicit data variable identified",
    "section": "Extreme ice impact loads",
    "source": "Ice Class Regulations and the Application Thereof",
    "sourceSheet": "TRAFICOM",
    "sourceText": "The thruster must withstand the loads occurring when the design ice block defined in Table 6-3 impacts on the thruster body when the ship is sailing at a typical ice operating speed. Load cases for impact loads are given in Table 6-16. The contact geometry is estimated to be hemispherical in shape. If the actual contact geometry differs from the shape of the hemisphere, a sphere radius must be estimated so that the growth of the contact area as a function of penetration of ice corresponds as closely as possible to the actual geometrical shape penetration.",
    "sourceUrl": "https://www.finlex.fi/en/authorities/regulations/traficom-transport-maritime/2021/47238"
  },
